{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The month of the aviv.</b> So called because there was aviv [grain in the stalk-stage] in it when they went out from Egypt. The deniers say that no Passover may be observed without aviv, and I have already refuted their nonsense. We too concede that the court would inspect for aviv. Know that the months have no names in the holy tongue, for Nisan, Sivan, Kislev, Tevet, and Adar — which are mentioned in Scripture — are in the Chaldean language; therefore it says, it is the month of Nisan. We find only Ziv, Ethanim, and Bul. And the sense of \"first\" is: wherever the aviv is found, that is the first month, for from there the counting of months begins. Whether the preceding year was twelve months or thirteen, we do not mind. And this is the sense of \"first.\" Only our predecessors of blessed memory interchanged with the aviv other considerations, and all their words are truth." "<b>By night.</b> He brought you out from under Pharaoh's jurisdiction. And the near one I shall yet explain."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Read העתיקו עם האביב as 'interchanged with the aviv,' i.e., they made other considerations co-determinate with the aviv; the phrase is somewhat compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:40.638203835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}